   "evidence": "grep: the only `Integrable` statements in the file are `DensityProfile.integrable` (line 100) and `integrable_woodsSaxonDensity_norm` (line 230); `integral_hardSphereDensity_norm` and `integral_gaussianDensity_norm` prove values only. `DensityProfile.integrable`'s proof is `Integrable.of_integral_ne_zero` plus `nuc.massNumber_pos.ne'`, so it does not generalise to `hardSphereDensity m R` for arbitrary `m`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Nuclei/Density/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add `integrable_hardSphereDensity_norm` (via `integrable_indicator_iff measurableSet_closedBall` and finiteness of `volume (closedBall 0 R)`) and `integrable_gaussianDensity_norm` (via the Mathlib Gaussian integrability lemma for `rexp (-b * \u2016v\u2016 ^ 2)`), and list them beside `integrable_woodsSaxonDensity_norm` in the module docstring's Main statements.",
   "issue": "Integrability over `Space` is exported only for Woods-Saxon (`integrable_woodsSaxonDensity_norm`); the hard-sphere and Gaussian profiles get only their integral value (`integral_hardSphereDensity_norm` line 145, `integral_gaussianDensity_norm` line 172), which `integral_indicator_const` and `GaussianFourier.integral_rexp_neg_mul_sq_norm` give without ever establishing integrability. `DensityProfile.integrable` (line 100) recovers it only for the bundled profiles, since its proof needs `\u222b = A \u2260 0`; for the raw profiles at general `m` (and at `m = 0`) there is nothing, yet the remainder of \u00a70.2 (`T_A(b) = \u222b \u03c1_A(b,z) dz`, `\u222b T_A d\u00b2b = A`) needs integrability of the 3D profile to apply Fubini.",
   "line": 230
  }
